---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: eprfs-epr-cli-src-recall-seams
purpose: >
  The native `epr-cli` crate source. One concrete concern is placed here rather than lifted to
  a policy: `flow/memory/recall/` (the bounded-evidence recall executor) is split by SEAM, never
  left to regrow as one file — Task 0.5 (2026-09-11) carved `journey.rs` out of a ~2,800-line
  `mod.rs`, and the `no_recall_module_exceeds_the_soft_line_ceiling` shape test
  (`recall::shape`, `mod.rs`) now pins every recall module under a 1,800-line soft ceiling.
rules:
  - id: recall-seams-stay-split
    class: inject
    when:
      write: "*.rs"
      contains-any:
        - "fn discover("
        - "trait Provider"
        - "fn render_first_screen("
        - "fn print_refusal("
        - "fn measure("
        - "fn excerpt("
        - "fn revalidate("
        - "fn refresh_selected("
        - "fn native_context("
        - "fn evidence_continuation("
        - "fn parse_bank("
    dedupe-of: "elohim/eprfs/epr-cli/src/flow/memory/recall/mod.rs (module doc) + each seam file's own top-of-file `//!` purpose line — the seam boundaries are already named where they live"
    why: >
      This is the recall executor (`src/flow/memory/recall/`) — a new function belongs where its
      concern already lives, not back into `mod.rs`. JOURNEY/STANDING (`journey.rs`, and a sibling
      `standing.rs` the day journey.rs itself would cross the 1,800-line ceiling): the session
      state machine — `execute`'s per-operation dispatch, `revalidate`, `refresh_selected`,
      `native_context`, `evidence_continuation`, continuation/receipt-retention helpers, orientation
      and edge lookups. DISCOVERY (`discovery.rs`): the deterministic local traversal — `discover`,
      `discover_scored`, outline/heading and question-term machinery. PROVIDERS (`providers.rs`):
      the `Provider` trait and its implementations (`local`, `mempalace`, `fixture`) — recipe-
      selected, never a source of authority. LENS (`lens.rs`, station 1): the `role@model ->
      LensLevel` table and lens resolution — not yet split out; a function shaping that table
      belongs there once it exists. RENDER (`render.rs`): turning a view into the human screen —
      `render`, `render_first_screen`, `render_outline`, `render_hits`. REFUSAL (`refusal.rs`): the
      one refusal envelope — what went wrong, which session, what to do. MEASURE (`measure.rs`):
      the paired deterministic footprint lens and the `measure` op. RECEIPTS (`receipts.rs`):
      bounded reads and receipt adoption — the only code that touches source bytes on a reader's
      behalf. QUESTIONS (`questions.rs`, station 3): the fixed question bank — `Question`,
      `ReachedWhen`, the wire-shape `Raw*` structs, and `parse_bank`, which turns a hand-authored
      `question_bank` file into real `elohim_epr_rea::Intent`s (a `Cid` cannot deserialize from a
      bare JSON string, so this is also where that detour lives). `mod.rs` itself stays
      dispatch-only: `Contract`, `Execution`, `Args`, `parse_args`, `run`, `usage`, the small
      `command`/`action`/`push_*` helpers, `encode`, `truncate`. Grep the target seam file's
      existing top-of-file `//!` purpose line before adding a function anywhere in this tree —
      that comment names the seam's boundary in its own words.
    retire-when: >
      never (a structural guardrail, not a teaching rule): the shape test enforces the ceiling on
      every module every test run, so a function still needs a seam to land in for as long as the
      split exists. Re-scope this rule's `why:` in place — don't retire it — the day a new seam
      file (`lens.rs`, `standing.rs`) is born, so the placement guide stays complete.
---

# `epr-cli/src` — the native CLI implementation

Everything `epr` runs natively lives under here. The one concrete rule bound at this level is the
recall executor's seam split (`flow/memory/recall/`): a session-state helper, a discovery
traversal, a provider implementation, a render, a refusal, a measure, a receipt, and a question
bank each have a home file, and the shape test keeps every one of those files under a 1,800-line
soft ceiling. See
`.claude/skills/elohim-epr-metafile/SKILL.md` for the governance vocabulary this manifest uses, and
`flow/memory/recall/mod.rs`'s own module doc for what the executor as a whole is for.
